// §217 — FINNISH, the explainer. Keyed by the English source (normalized
// innerHTML for rich blocks, text for plate labels); see src/explain-i18n.js
// for why.
//
// Vocabulary is the SAME register the chrome and the primer use (src/i18n.js,
// src/primer-i18n.fi.js), one name per part: koneisto, sveitsiläinen
// ankkurikäynti, ankkuripyörä, ankkuri (the pallet fork AND the alarm
// governor's anchor), liipotin, hiusjousi, vetojousi, jousikotelo, fusee (the
// loan, compounded with a hyphen: fusee-kartio, fusee-ketju), ketju, pinioni,
// vetonuppi, pilaripyörä, herätyksen säädin (never a bare «säädin», which would
// read as the timekeeping regulator). The project's own words — the Vocabulary
// table's thirty — are coined once here: asema, korkeusvyöhyke, kerros /
// kaista, käytävä, marginaali (the one margin; «välys» for a clearance),
// atsimuutti, rengasalue, jänne, tangentti, liikematka (a throw), verhopinta,
// yksikkö, syöte (an axis: «akseli» is the arbor), asento / asennoitu, rivi,
// portti, alaraja / budjetti, luovutus, vapautus, toimintoryhmä, suora,
// taitto, haara (a fork), kulma, välipyörä, johdettu.
//
// Finnish attaches a case ending to a quoted identifier or a numeral with a
// COLON, and it rides OUTSIDE the span — `<code>CLEAR_MARGIN</code>:n`,
// `270°:n` — Finnish orthography's own rule for a token, and the one that
// keeps the <code> gate byte-identical. The hidden .gloss-variants rows list
// the case forms the prose actually uses, read off this table's own text.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED — they are the source constants this
// page exists to quote, so 0.15 keeps its point here as in every locale.
// Emphasis the English carries as CAPITALS rides the wording, never an added
// tag. «mallinnettu» vs «simuloitu» tracks the repo's modelled/simulated
// distinction exactly; HONESTY.fi gates it, and the noun «malli» (the credit
// line's tekoälymalli) is deliberately not the honesty word.
//
// Drafted by machine, not reviewed by a native speaker: the terms a workshop
// may dispute are listed in tools/l10n-review/questions.mjs.
